# oracle: pair_style smtbq with the TiO2 potential (ffield.smtbq.TiO2, QEqAll) on a 75-atom rutile cluster (the create_atoms cell of examples/PACKAGES/smtbq/in.smtbq.TiO2, a 4.5937, c 2.9587, 2 Ti and 4 O per cell, 2x2x2 cells; the example has 6x6x11 periodic cells), free boundaries (boundary f f f, so the 12.17 A cutoff does not make hundreds of periodic images), read from w189sq_tio2_cluster.data; 10 NVE steps from 300 K with the example's charge computes; Nevery 1, so the charges are equilibrated inside the pair style every step
# native: LAMMPS b332f28 built from source with -D PKG_SMTBQ=on -D PKG_MANYBODY=on -D PKG_KSPACE=on -D PKG_MOLECULE=on -D PKG_EXTRA-FIX=on (the scratch build of the SMTBQ package, the installed lmp has no SMTBQ)
# oracle-inputs: w189sq_tio2_cluster.data
# oracle-potentials: ffield.smtbq.TiO2
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
# Measured with native LAMMPS: thermo max relative error 1.4e-12, per-atom 1.6e-11 (QEq every step; engine ~2.2 s).
units           metal
atom_style      charge
dimension       3
boundary        f f f
read_data       w189sq_tio2_cluster.data
mass            1 16.00
mass            2 47.867
group           Oxy type 1
compute         chargeOxy Oxy property/atom q
compute         q_Oxy Oxy reduce ave c_chargeOxy
group           Ti type 2
compute         chargeTi Ti property/atom q
compute         q_Ti Ti reduce ave c_chargeTi
velocity        all create 300 277387
pair_style      smtbq
pair_coeff      * * ffield.smtbq.TiO2 O Ti
neighbor        0.5 bin
neigh_modify    every 20 delay 0 check yes
timestep        0.0002
thermo_style    custom step temp press pe ke etotal c_q_Ti c_q_Oxy lx ly lz vol
thermo_modify   format float %.15g flush yes
thermo          1
fix             3 all nve
run             10
